BIT-02: Evaluate each term and formula once per rate evaluation, from flat expressions

Most of the run time was the expression interpreter re-doing work. Each
expression was a linked list of tokens, evaluated with an 8 KB stack array
per call; every NaN check was a call into another file; every variable was
fetched through a callback that decoded its kind; and every reference to a
[TERMS] entry or formula species evaluated it again, recursively. Store each
expression in one block, check for NaN inline, skip per-segment copies that
are never used, and evaluate every term and formula once per rate
evaluation into an array that expressions read directly. The same
operations are done in the same order.

Also: with interpreted chemistry, a cycle of formula species (or of terms
that the input check misses), which recursed until the stack overflowed, is
now reported as error 506 by MSXopen. With the COMPILER option, such term
cycles still overflow the stack.

Requires: none
Results: identical (every concentration, the output file and the report are unchanged)

Apply from the root of an EPANET-MSX checkout at 85a303d, after FIX-01, FIX-02 and BIT-01:
    git apply --whitespace=nowarn BIT-02.patch
or use tools/build-msx.sh, which applies the series in order.

